{%- comment -%}
  Where a design with no page of its own sends a shopper: the catalog, already
  narrowed to that design.

  Two mechanisms are in the one link on purpose. `filter.v.option.<name>` is
  Shopify's own filter, applied on the server across the whole catalog when
  Search & Discovery has a filter for that option. `#design=<handle>` is read by
  catalog-filters.js, which preselects the same design in the rail's built-in
  buttons when it does not. Whichever the store has, the shopper lands on the
  design; a store with neither lands on the full catalog, which is the honest
  worst case rather than a dead end.

  Usage: {% render 'design-url', name: 'Ekdali', option: 'Design' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign opt_param = option | default: 'Design' | downcase | url_encode
  assign val_param = name | url_encode
  assign key = name | handle
  echo routes.all_products_collection_url | append: '?filter.v.option.' | append: opt_param | append: '=' | append: val_param | append: '#design=' | append: key
-%}
